Once they flowed like sand between my fingers,
every grain something tangible I could touch,
something I could feel.

My hands are cold now and my fingers don't work.
My mind is much the same — no vivid colours, nothing.
I am spent.

I once would speak to someone. Close. Near or far.
Now it's just me. They have all moved on.
My orbit has decayed.

I once had the feeling of being complete —
shared joys, smiles, and life.
I am now a husk.
